WEBVTT

00:00.660 --> 00:04.430
Show 109% by shading.

00:04.430 --> 00:09.760
So just as a bit of review, 109%
if we were to write it

00:09.760 --> 00:16.910
out, would literally be 109
percent, which is the same

00:16.910 --> 00:25.330
thing as 109 per-- and I could
write cent again, but that's

00:25.330 --> 00:26.270
getting old.

00:26.270 --> 00:28.540
Cent means 100, so it literally

00:28.540 --> 00:32.850
means 109 per hundred.

00:32.850 --> 00:35.400
If you had 100 per 100, you're
dealing with the whole, but

00:35.400 --> 00:37.040
now we have more than a whole.

00:37.040 --> 00:38.850
We have 109 per 100.

00:38.850 --> 00:41.460
We can actually write this as
a ratio, or as a fraction.

00:41.460 --> 00:45.730
This is the same thing
as 109 per 100.

00:45.730 --> 00:48.220
It's the the same thing
as 109/100.

00:48.220 --> 00:50.260
So let's shade that in.

00:50.260 --> 00:53.720
So we have a whole here,
so we could consider

00:53.720 --> 00:55.300
this square a whole.

00:55.300 --> 00:57.150
In the last video, we counted.

00:57.150 --> 00:58.830
This is a 10 by 10 square.

00:58.830 --> 01:01.460
It is cut up into 100 pieces.

01:01.460 --> 01:05.510
So if we want 109 of those
100 pieces, what

01:05.510 --> 01:06.660
are we talking about?

01:06.660 --> 01:08.130
That means we're going to
shade in all of the

01:08.130 --> 01:09.350
100 right over here.

01:09.350 --> 01:10.950
Let me do that in a new color.

01:10.950 --> 01:13.090
So we'll shade in all of this.

01:17.550 --> 01:20.740
If you just shaded that in,
that would be 100%.

01:20.740 --> 01:28.410
That would be 100/100, or
100 per 100, or 100%.

01:28.410 --> 01:30.540
I think you're getting the
meaning of all of this.

01:30.540 --> 01:31.940
I don't just want you just
memorize this stuff.

01:31.940 --> 01:34.970
This really just means 100
out of 100, or a whole.

01:34.970 --> 01:37.540
And you can see that this
is the whole square.

01:37.540 --> 01:39.010
That's 100 out of
100 right there.

01:39.010 --> 01:43.200
The question is saying show
us 109% by shading.

01:43.200 --> 01:46.610
We already did 100 per 100, but
we need to do another 9,

01:46.610 --> 01:48.170
so let's shade in another 9.

01:48.170 --> 01:55.380
So now we have one, two, three,
four, five, six, seven,

01:55.380 --> 01:57.030
eight, nine.

01:57.030 --> 01:59.350
So this piece right here, you
could almost view that is--

01:59.350 --> 02:02.090
well, that is!

02:02.090 --> 02:04.320
That is 9% of an
entire square.

02:04.320 --> 02:06.700
This is 100% of an
entire square.

02:06.700 --> 02:10.620
If you considered this whole
thing plus this blue area

02:10.620 --> 02:16.920
right over here, you are talking
about 109% of one

02:16.920 --> 02:18.690
whole square.

02:18.690 --> 02:21.430
Hopefully, that made sense.
